{"id":"word:hebrew:H4886","type":"word","title":"מָשַׁח","subtitle":"H4886 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to rub with oil , i.e. to anoint ; by implication, to consecrate ; also to paint","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מָשַׁח (H4886) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 69 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מָשַׁח (mâshach) means to rub with oil , i.e. to anoint ; by implication, to consecrate ; also to paint First listed occurrence: 1Chr 11 3."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מָשַׁח","transliteration":"mâshach","pronunciation":"maw-shakh'","strong":"H4886","lemmaId":"hebrew:H4886","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וּ/מָשַׁחְתָּ֥","מְשֻׁחִ֣ים","הִמָּשַׁ֣ח","וַ/יִּמְשְׁח֧וּ","תִּמְשַׁ֥ח"],"morphs":[["HC/Vqq2ms",11],["HC/Vqw3mp",6],["HC/Vqw3ms",6],["HVqp1cs/Sp2ms",4],["HVqsmpa",4],["HVNc",4],["HVqp3cp",3],["HVqi2ms",3],["HVqp3ms/Sp2ms",2],["HC/Vqw3mp/Sp3ms",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"to rub with oil , i.e. to anoint ; by implication, to consecrate ; also to paint","usage":"anoint, paint.","full":"H4886. mashach מָשַׁח verb smear, anoint (Late Hebrew id. ; originally probably as Arabic wipe or stroke with the hand (compare RS Semitic i. 215; 2nd ed., 283 ), anoint, Aramaic מְשַׁח anoint ; on משת , id. (?) in Aramaic inscription see CIS ii.1. No.145, C, 1 ; Palmyrene משחא oil Vog No.16 ; Ethiopic anoint, feast, dine Di Lex 176 ; (Assyrian mašâ—u is measure; Aramaic מְשַׁח id. ; Arabic measurement , compare Dl Prol. 178 Frä 282 )); — Qal Perfect 3masculine singular ׳מ Num 3:25 2 t.; suffix מְשָֽׁחֲךָ Psa 45:8 ; 1Sam 10:1 ; מְשָׁחוֺ 2Chr 22:7 ; 2 masculine singular מָשַׁחְתָּ Gen 31:13 12 t., + 9 t. Perfect; Imperfect 3masculine singular יִמְשַׁח Lev 16:32 6 t.; 3 masculine plural יִמְשָׁ֑חוּ Amos 6:6 , + 13 t. Imperfect; Imperative suffix מְשָׁחֵהוּ 1Sam 16:12 ; plural מִשְׁחוּ Isa 21:5 ; Infinitive absolute מָשׁוֺחַ Jer 22:14 ; construct מְשֹׁחַ Judg 9:8 ; Dan 9:24 + Hosea 8:3 ᵐ5 We GASm Now; מָשְׁחָה Exod 29:29 ; suffix מְשׁחֳךָ 1Sam 15:1 (Baer); מָשְׁחוֺ Lev 7:36 ; מָשְׁחָתָם Exod 40:15 ; Participle plural משְׁחִים Judg 9:15 ; passive מָשׁוּחַ 2Sam 3:39 (We suggests derivation from שׁח , defective משׁח ( מֻשַׁח ), wrongly read as מָשֻׁחַ ; or by transposition משׁוח may have been mistaken for an unexampled מוּשַׁח Hoph`al Participle of שׁוח ); מָשִׁיחַ 1:21 (but read מָשֻׁח (or נמשׁח ) Manuscripts We Dr Kit Bu HPS); plural מְשֻׁחִים Exod 29:2 4 t; — 1 smear , house with colour (paint) Jer 22:14 ; shield with oil (anoint) Isa 21:5 ; 2Sam 1:21 (compare Dr; Gr מָשׁוּחַ כְּלִי weapon anointed ; Peters JBL 893, 56 מָשׁוּחַ כְּלֵי weapons of one (the king) anointed ); the person, with ointments Amos 6:6 ; unleavened cakes, with oil Exod 29:2 ; Lev 2:4 ; Num 6:15 (P). 2 anoint , as consecration, solemn setting apart to an office, always by the use of oil poured on the head: לנביא as a prophet 1Kin 19:16 (Elisha by Elijah) Isa 61:1 ; elsewhere of king, with accusative, מֶלֶךְ Judg 9:8 (E), so Hosea 8:3 reading מֶלֶךְ מִמְּשֹׁחַ (for מ ׳מִמַּשָּׂא ᵑ0 ) We GASm Now; also 7:3 reading יִמְשְׁחוּ (for יְשַׂמְּחוּ ᵑ0 ) We Now; elsewhere accusative of person 1Sam 16:3 , 12 , 13 ; 1Kin 1:39 ; 2Kin 11:12 ; 23:30 ; 2Chr 22:7 ; 23:11 ; קָדְשִׁי בְּשֶׁמֶן Psa 89:21 with my holy oil ; שָׂשׂוֺן שׁמן 45:8 (figurative); with על , 2Sam 19:11 whom we have anointed over us; לְמֶלֶךְ 1Kin 1:45 ; 5:15 ; with לְמֶלֶךְ עַל, Judg 9:15 ; 2Sam 2:4 , 7 ; 1Kin 19:15 ; ישׂראל על over Israel 1Sam 15:1 , 17 ; 2Sam 5:3 = 1Chr 11:3 ; 2Sam 5:17 ; 12:7 ; 1Kin 1:34 ; 19:16 ; אֶליֿשׂראל 2Kin 9:3 , 6 , 12 (Ehpraimitic source); לנגיד 1Chr 29:22 ; על 1Sam 9:16 ; 10:1 ; מֶלֶךְ מָשׁוּחַ 2Sam 3:39 (? see above) 3 anoint, consecrate to religious service: a. Aaronic priests , only P, with accusative of person Exod 28:41 ; 29:7 ; 30:30 ; 40:13 , 15 (3 t. in verse); Lev 7:36 ; 8:12 ; 16:32 ; absolute Exod 29:29 ; הַמְּשֻׁחִים הכהנים Num 3:3 . b. sacred things: מַצֵּבָה Gen 31:13 (E); tabernacle and its sacred vessels Exod 29:36 ; 30:26 ; 40:9-10 , 11 ; Lev 8:10-11 , (all P); קדשׁים קדשׁ Dan 9:24 . Niph`al Perfect 3masculine singular נִמְשַׁח 1Chr 14:8 ; Infinitive הִמָּשַׁח Lev 6:13 3 t; — be anointed , ישׂראל כל על למלך 1Chr 14:8 ; Aaron and his sons Lev 6:13 (P); altar Num 7:10 , 84 , 88 . מְשַׁח noun [masculine] oil (see Biblical Hebrew); — absolute Ezra 6:9 ; 7:22 . [ מִשְׁכַּב ] see שׁכב . [ מִשְׁכַּן ] see שׁכן . [ מַשְׁרוֺקִית ] see שׁרק . [ מִשְׁתֶּה ] see שׁתּה . [ מַתְּנָא ] see נתן .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 11 3","keyReferences":["1Chr 11 3","1Chr 14 8","1Chr 29 22","1Kgs 1 34","1Kgs 1 39","1Kgs 1 45","1Kgs 5 15","1Kgs 19 15"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":69,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 11 3","book":"1Chr","chapter":11,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּמְשְׁח֨וּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3mp"},{"reference":"1Chr 14 8","book":"1Chr","chapter":14,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נִמְשַׁ֨ח","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVNp3ms"},{"reference":"1Chr 29 22","book":"1Chr","chapter":29,"verse":22,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּמְשְׁח֧וּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3mp"},{"reference":"1Kgs 1 34","book":"1Kgs","chapter":1,"verse":34,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/מָשַׁ֣ח","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqq3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 1 39","book":"1Kgs","chapter":1,"verse":39,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּמְשַׁ֖ח","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 1 45","book":"1Kgs","chapter":1,"verse":45,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּמְשְׁח֣וּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3mp"},{"reference":"1Kgs 5 15","book":"1Kgs","chapter":5,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מָשְׁח֥וּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqp3cp"},{"reference":"1Kgs 19 15","book":"1Kgs","chapter":19,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"ו